From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 08:28:17 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] v4l2: decode to the raw format the client asks for

A decoder lists the colour formats it produces from the raw pixel format
parameter of its output, which the decoder interface did not define, so
MediaCodecInfo showed no 10-bit format for a Main 10 decoder. The
component also took whatever format the device announced: a 10-bit
stream came out as P010 for a client that asked for flexible YUV and
could not take 10 bits.

The interface now defines the parameter, with flexible YUV 4:2:0 as its
default and P010 added for the profiles that have 10-bit samples. The
decoder is told the format the client chose and, for a client that
wants 8-bit YUV, asks the device for an 8-bit planar capture format in
place of P010 when the device offers one. A client that asks for P010
gets the device's own format, and a stream with 8-bit samples is
unaffected.
---
